{"summary":"Accepted only fr-5-b7289131. The legacy kinetic `_mg` compatibility issue is real in alias-only deserialization paths, even though some loader/migration paths already convert correctly. Rejected the other two because they are based on outdated premises or describe cleanup rather than a concrete correctness defect.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-b737f90d","decision":"reject","rationale":"`legacy_process_param_normalization()` currently returns `None` for all of the cited process params, so the claimed unit/value mismatch does not actually occur here. Removing `_unit` would be harmless cleanup, but this is not a substantive correctness issue in the current code."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-60828312","decision":"reject","rationale":"The cited rename fallout is stale. The current `ProcessParamsPreset` validation paths and `tank_scenarios` materialization already reference the canonical `*_mg_c_per_l` / `*_mg_n_per_l` / `*_mg_per_l` fields, and the present compile failure is elsewhere (`HabitatEnv.depth_attenuation`), not from these field names."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-b7289131","decision":"accept","rationale":"The amendment overstates the gap because `parse_process_params_preset()` and the save-schema migration already convert legacy kinetic `_mg` keys. But the underlying problem is real: public alias-only deserialization paths on `ProcessParams` / `ProcessParamsPreset` still give legacy `_mg` payloads the wrong semantics (and one preset alias is inconsistent), so compatibility should rely on an actual migration/conversion path rather than raw aliases."}]}